<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">

    <!-- Hero: what it is, how to get it. The terminal below does the rest. -->
    <section class="pt-16 pb-10 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-12">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-soft">HTTP/2 reverse proxy &middot; written in Rust &middot; MIT</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] leading-[1.05] text-fg text-balance">
            A reverse proxy you can watch.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-soft text-pretty">
            Soli Proxy terminates TLS, routes HTTP/2 and WebSockets, and runs your apps itself:
            blue-green deploys, sleep when idle, wake on the next request. Its terminal UI shows
            every one of those as it happens.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mt-8 flex w-fit max-w-full items-center gap-3 rounded-md bg-panel py-2 pl-4 pr-2 font-mono text-[13px]" style="box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule)">
            <span class="select-none text-muted" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <code class="no-scrollbar min-w-0 flex-1 overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap text-fg">curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/solisoft/soli-proxy/main/install.sh | sh</code>
            <button type="button" onclick="copyCode(this)" class="btn !px-2 !py-1 text-xs text-soft hover:text-fg">copy</button>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
            <a href="/docs/getting-started" class="btn btn-primary">Getting started</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/solisoft/soli-proxy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link font-mono text-sm">github.com/solisoft/soli-proxy</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The terminal UI, replayed by public/js/tui.js. -->
    <section aria-labelledby="tui-heading">
        <h2 id="tui-heading" class="sr-only">The terminal UI</h2>
        <!-- data-version: the sidebar's version line. Bump it with each release. -->
        <div id="tui" class="term" data-version="1.13.0" tabindex="0"
             aria-label="Replica of the Soli Proxy terminal UI. Press m to pause or resume the motion.">
            <div class="term-bar">
                <span>soli-proxy tui</span>
                <span>proxy.example.com</span>
            </div>
            <div class="term-screen" role="img"
                 aria-label="The dashboard: requests flow from clients through soli-proxy to five apps. Shop deploys to its green slot, blog wakes from sleep, a scanner is banned, crm closes for maintenance and api throws 502s, each step listed in the events journal.">
                <span class="term-probe" aria-hidden="true">0000000000</span>
                <pre aria-hidden="true"></pre>
                <noscript>
                    <p class="p-6 font-mono text-sm text-soft">The replay needs JavaScript. The <a class="link" href="/docs/getting-started">getting started guide</a> shows the real thing: <code>soli-proxy tui</code>.</p>
                </noscript>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 font-mono text-xs text-soft">
            <span id="tui-status" aria-live="off">01/05 &middot; blue-green deploy</span>
            <button type="button" id="tui-motion" aria-pressed="true" class="btn !px-2 !py-1 text-xs text-soft hover:text-fg">
                <kbd class="text-accent">m</kbd> motion <span data-state>on</span>
            </button>
        </div>

        <!-- What the loop shows, in order. The playing one is marked by tui.js;
             each title seeks the replay to it. -->
        <ol id="tui-chapters" class="mt-10 grid gap-x-6 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
            <li class="chapter pl-4" data-chapter data-title="blue-green deploy" aria-current="step">
                <button type="button" data-seek="0" class="chapter-seek text-left">
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted">01</span>
                    <span class="chapter-title mt-1 block font-medium text-soft">Blue-green deploy</span>
                </button>
                <p class="chapter-body mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">
                    <kbd class="font-mono text-accent">D</kbd> on an app, or <code class="text-fg">soli-proxy deploy shop</code>.
                    The idle slot starts, passes its health check, takes the traffic, and the old one drains.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/apps#cli-commands" class="link mt-2 inline-block font-mono text-xs">apps &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li class="chapter pl-4" data-chapter data-title="scale to zero">
                <button type="button" data-seek="1" class="chapter-seek text-left">
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted">02</span>
                    <span class="chapter-title mt-1 block font-medium text-soft">Scale to zero</span>
                </button>
                <p class="chapter-body mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">
                    blog was idle, so it was stopped and holds no memory. The next request starts it and waits
                    for it: a slower first byte, not an error.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/apps#scale-to-zero" class="link mt-2 inline-block font-mono text-xs">idle_timeout &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li class="chapter pl-4" data-chapter data-title="bots and traps">
                <button type="button" data-seek="2" class="chapter-seek text-left">
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted">03</span>
                    <span class="chapter-title mt-1 block font-medium text-soft">Bots and traps</span>
                </button>
                <p class="chapter-body mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">
                    A scanner asks for <code class="text-fg">/.env</code> and is banned from every site at once.
                    Search engines pass, and a page&rsquo;s own requests never ban a visitor.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/configuration#bots" class="link mt-2 inline-block font-mono text-xs">[bots] &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li class="chapter pl-4" data-chapter data-title="maintenance">
                <button type="button" data-seek="3" class="chapter-seek text-left">
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted">04</span>
                    <span class="chapter-title mt-1 block font-medium text-soft">Maintenance</span>
                </button>
                <p class="chapter-body mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">
                    <kbd class="font-mono text-accent">M</kbd> closes crm until 18:30. Visitors get a page in their
                    language that reloads itself when it reopens.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/configuration#maintenance" class="link mt-2 inline-block font-mono text-xs">maintenance &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li class="chapter pl-4" data-chapter data-title="errors as they happen">
                <button type="button" data-seek="4" class="chapter-seek text-left">
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted">05</span>
                    <span class="chapter-title mt-1 block font-medium text-soft">Errors as they happen</span>
                </button>
                <p class="chapter-body mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">
                    api answers 502. Its line carries red packets, the 5xx rate turns red, and each failure
                    lands in the journal with its path.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/admin-api" class="link mt-2 inline-block font-mono text-xs">admin api &rarr;</a>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- One file per app -->
    <section class="mt-24 sm:mt-32 border-t border-rule pt-12" aria-labelledby="apps-heading">
        <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
            <div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-4">
                <h2 id="apps-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">One file per app</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 text-soft leading-relaxed text-pretty">
                    A directory in <code class="text-fg">sites/</code>, named after the domain, with an
                    <code class="text-fg">app.infos</code> in it. The proxy finds it, gives it a port and a
                    certificate, health-checks it and starts sending it traffic. No container registry, no YAML.
                </p>
                <a href="/docs/apps" class="link mt-4 inline-block font-mono text-sm">every app.infos key &rarr;</a>
            </div>
            <div class="grid min-w-0 gap-4 lg:col-span-8 md:grid-cols-2">
                <figure class="min-w-0 rounded-md bg-panel" style="box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule)">
                    <figcaption class="border-b border-rule px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-soft">sites/shop.example.com/app.infos</figcaption>
<pre class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-4 text-[13px] leading-6 text-fg"><code>name = <span class="ts">"shop"</span>
domain = <span class="ts">"shop.example.com"</span>
start_script = <span class="ts">"bin/server --port $PORT"</span>
health_check = <span class="ts">"/health"</span>
idle_timeout = <span class="tn">1800</span>  <span class="tc"># asleep after 30 min</span></code></pre>
                </figure>
                <figure class="min-w-0 rounded-md bg-panel" style="box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule)">
                    <figcaption class="border-b border-rule px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-soft">shell</figcaption>
<pre class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-4 text-[13px] leading-6 text-fg"><code><span class="tc">$</span> soli-proxy check
<span class="tc">  # every config and app.infos, no port bound</span>
<span class="tc">$</span> soli-proxy <span class="tk">-d</span>
<span class="tc">  # start in the background</span>
<span class="tc">$</span> soli-proxy deploy shop
<span class="tc">  # blue-green, nothing dropped</span>
<span class="tc">$</span> soli-proxy tui</code></pre>
                </figure>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The rest, listed plainly. -->
    <section class="mt-24 sm:mt-32 border-t border-rule pt-12" aria-labelledby="more-heading">
        <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
            <h2 id="more-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg lg:col-span-4">Also in the binary</h2>
            <dl class="grid gap-x-10 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:col-span-8">
                <div class="border-t border-rule py-5">
                    <dt class="font-medium text-fg">Automatic TLS</dt>
                    <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">Self-signed certificates in development, Let&rsquo;s Encrypt in production over ACME HTTP-01, one per domain by SNI, renewal checked every 12 hours.</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="border-t border-rule py-5">
                    <dt class="font-medium text-fg">Restarts nobody notices</dt>
                    <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">Apps outlive the proxy and the next one adopts them. Under the systemd socket unit, connections wait in the kernel queue instead of being refused.</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="border-t border-rule py-5">
                    <dt class="font-medium text-fg">WebSockets</dt>
                    <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">Proxied both ways, so live reload and real-time apps work behind it unchanged.</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="border-t border-rule py-5">
                    <dt class="font-medium text-fg">Config reload</dt>
                    <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">Applied without a restart: on SIGUSR1, through the admin API, or when the file watcher sees the change.</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="border-t border-rule py-5">
                    <dt class="font-medium text-fg">Lua 5.4 hooks</dt>
                    <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">Auth, routing, response rewriting and logging, per route or global. Nothing runs, and nothing is paid, without a script.</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="border-t border-rule py-5">
                    <dt class="font-medium text-fg">Circuit breakers, Prometheus</dt>
                    <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soft">A breaker per backend with failover, and a <code class="text-fg">/metrics</code> endpoint for Grafana.</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- One number, with its source. -->
    <section class="mt-24 sm:mt-32 border-t border-rule pt-12" aria-labelledby="bench-heading">
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-baseline">
            <h2 id="bench-heading" class="font-mono text-5xl sm:text-6xl font-medium tracking-tight text-fg tabular-nums lg:col-span-4">54&thinsp;ns</h2>
            <p class="max-w-xl text-soft leading-relaxed lg:col-span-8">
                to match a request against the routing table, measured with Criterion.
                <a href="/docs/benchmark" class="link">The benchmark page</a> has the method and the rest of the numbers.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Docs -->
    <section class="mt-24 sm:mt-32 mb-24 border-t border-rule pt-12" aria-labelledby="docs-heading">
        <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
            <h2 id="docs-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg lg:col-span-4">Documentation</h2>
            <ul class="lg:col-span-8 divide-y divide-[color:var(--rule)] border-y border-rule">
                <li><a href="/docs/getting-started" class="group flex flex-col gap-1 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-fg sm:w-44 shrink-0">getting started <span class="text-accent opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-150 group-hover:opacity-100">&rarr;</span></span><span class="text-sm text-soft">Install, write a proxy.conf, serve your first app over HTTPS.</span></a></li>
                <li><a href="/docs/apps" class="group flex flex-col gap-1 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-fg sm:w-44 shrink-0">apps <span class="text-accent opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-150 group-hover:opacity-100">&rarr;</span></span><span class="text-sm text-soft">app.infos, blue-green deploys, scale to zero, per-environment settings.</span></a></li>
                <li><a href="/docs/configuration" class="group flex flex-col gap-1 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-fg sm:w-44 shrink-0">configuration <span class="text-accent opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-150 group-hover:opacity-100">&rarr;</span></span><span class="text-sm text-soft">Routing rules, config.toml, maintenance, bots.</span></a></li>
                <li><a href="/docs/admin-api" class="group flex flex-col gap-1 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-fg sm:w-44 shrink-0">admin api <span class="text-accent opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-150 group-hover:opacity-100">&rarr;</span></span><span class="text-sm text-soft">Apps, routes, metrics and the event stream the TUI draws from.</span></a></li>
                <li><a href="/docs/scripting" class="group flex flex-col gap-1 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-fg sm:w-44 shrink-0">scripting <span class="text-accent opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-150 group-hover:opacity-100">&rarr;</span></span><span class="text-sm text-soft">Four Lua hook points: auth, routing, responses, logging.</span></a></li>
                <li><a href="/docs/security" class="group flex flex-col gap-1 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-fg sm:w-44 shrink-0">security <span class="text-accent opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-150 group-hover:opacity-100">&rarr;</span></span><span class="text-sm text-soft">ACME certificates, circuit breakers, failover.</span></a></li>
                <li><a href="/docs/deployment" class="group flex flex-col gap-1 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-fg sm:w-44 shrink-0">deployment <span class="text-accent opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-150 group-hover:opacity-100">&rarr;</span></span><span class="text-sm text-soft">Docker, Compose, a daemon or a systemd unit.</span></a></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
